  "milestone_brief": "### desktop-distribution-spike-3 \u2014 Prove safe desktop sidecar lifecycle\n\n**Question.** Can the shared desktop supervisor safely own exactly one local server across normal launch, duplicate launch, timeout, child crash, supervisor crash, and shutdown on macOS?\n\n**Timebox.** At most 3 days. Fixture sidecar and protocol decision only.\n\n**Acceptance criteria.**\n- Exercise Tauri sidecar spawning, single-instance activation, dynamic loopback-port handoff, and readiness polling with a fixture process.\n- Exercise graceful stop, bounded forced kill, child crash, parent crash, and orphan/listener detection.\n- Confirm secrets are not passed in command-line arguments or written to logs and the server never binds non-loopback.\n- Measure 30 launch/stop cycles and record orphan/listener count.\n- Record the lifecycle protocol, OS primitives, and fallback if Tauri cannot enforce the contract.\n\n**Dependencies.** None.\n\n**GitHub issue.** chris-dare-dev/arXMCP#386.",
